<?php

return [
    // Breadcrumbs & titles
    'Business logic vulnerabilities' => 'Kerentanan logika bisnis',
    'Examples' => 'Contoh kasus',
    'Examples of business logic vulnerabilities' => 'Contoh kerentanan logika bisnis',
    'Note' => 'Catatan',
    'More information' => 'Informasi lebih lanjut',

    // Overview page
    "In this section, we'll introduce the concept of business logic vulnerabilities and explain how they can arise due to flawed assumptions about user behavior. We'll discuss the potential impact of logic flaws and teach you how they can be exploited. You can also practice what you've learned using our interactive labs, which are based on real bugs that we've encountered in the wild. Finally, we'll provide some general best practices to help you prevent these kinds of logic flaws arising in your own applications." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami memperkenalkan konsep kerentanan logika bisnis serta cara kemunculannya akibat asumsi keliru terhadap perilaku pengguna. Anda akan mempelajari dampaknya, teknik eksploitasi lewat lab interaktif berbasis kasus nyata, serta praktik pencegahan terbaik.',
    "If you're already familiar with the basic concepts behind business logic vulnerabilities and just want to practice exploiting them on some realistic, deliberately vulnerable targets, you can access all of the labs in this topic from the link below." => 'Jika Anda sudah memahami dasar kerentanan logika bisnis dan ingin langsung berlatih eksploitasi pada target simulasi yang rentan, akses semua lab pada topik ini melalui tautan berikut.',
    'View all business logic vulnerabilities labs' => 'Lihat semua lab kerentanan logika bisnis',
    'What are business logic vulnerabilities?' => 'Apa itu kerentanan logika bisnis?',
    'Business logic vulnerabilities are flaws in the design and implementation of an application that allow an attacker to elicit unintended behavior. This potentially enables attackers to manipulate legitimate functionality to achieve a malicious goal. These flaws are generally the result of failing to anticipate unusual application states that may occur and, consequently, failing to handle them safely.' => 'Kerentanan logika bisnis adalah cacat pada desain maupun implementasi aplikasi yang memungkinkan penyerang memicu perilaku tak terduga dan memanipulasi fitur sah untuk tujuan berbahaya. Masalah ini umumnya muncul karena aplikasi gagal mengantisipasi kondisi penggunaan yang tidak lazim.',
    'In this context, the term "business logic" simply refers to the set of rules that define how the application operates. As these rules aren\'t always directly related to a business, the associated vulnerabilities are also known as "application logic vulnerabilities" or simply "logic flaws".' => 'Dalam konteks ini, "logika bisnis" merujuk pada sekumpulan aturan yang mengatur cara kerja aplikasi. Karena aturannya tidak selalu berkaitan dengan proses komersial, celah ini kerap disebut pula "celah logika aplikasi" atau "logic flaws".',
    "Logic flaws are often invisible to people who aren't explicitly looking for them as they typically won't be exposed by normal use of the application. However, an attacker may be able to exploit behavioral quirks by interacting with the application in ways that developers never intended." => 'Cacat logika sering luput terlihat saat pemakaian normal. Penyerang memanfaatkannya dengan berinteraksi menggunakan skenario yang tidak pernah dibayangkan pengembang.',
    "One of the main purposes of business logic is to enforce the rules and constraints that were defined when designing the application or functionality. Broadly speaking, the business rules dictate how the application should react when a given scenario occurs. This includes preventing users from doing things that will have a negative impact on the business or that simply don't make sense." => 'Salah satu fungsi utama logika bisnis adalah menegakkan aturan dan batasan sistem agar pengguna tidak dapat melakukan aksi yang merugikan atau tidak masuk akal.',
    "Flaws in the logic can allow attackers to circumvent these rules. For example, they might be able to complete a transaction without going through the intended purchase workflow. In other cases, broken or non-existent validation of user-supplied data might allow users to make arbitrary changes to transaction-critical values or submit nonsensical input. By passing unexpected values into server-side logic, an attacker can potentially induce the application to do something that it isn't supposed to." => 'Celah pada logika memungkinkan penyerang melewati batasan tersebut, misalnya menyelesaikan transaksi tanpa alur pembayaran penuh atau mengubah angka transaksi penting dengan mengirimkan nilai tidak wajar ke logika server.',
    "Logic-based vulnerabilities can be extremely diverse and are often unique to the application and its specific functionality. Identifying them often requires a certain amount of human knowledge, such as an understanding of the business domain or what goals an attacker might have in a given context. This makes them difficult to detect using automated vulnerability scanners. As a result, logic flaws are a great target for bug bounty hunters and manual testers in general." => 'Kerentanan logika sangat bervariasi dan spesifik terhadap konteks aplikasi. Karena pemindai otomatis sulit memahaminya, pengujian manual dan pemahaman proses bisnis menjadi kunci untuk menemukannya.',
    'How do business logic vulnerabilities arise?' => 'Bagaimana kerentanan logika bisnis muncul?',
    'Business logic vulnerabilities often arise because the design and development teams make flawed assumptions about how users will interact with the application. These bad assumptions can lead to inadequate validation of user input. For example, if the developers assume that users will pass data exclusively via a web browser, the application may rely entirely on weak client-side controls to validate input. These are easily bypassed by an attacker using an intercepting proxy.' => 'Cacat logika bisnis kerap bersumber dari asumsi keliru mengenai cara pengguna memakai aplikasi, seperti mengandalkan validasi di sisi klien saja karena mengira semua masukan datang apa adanya dari peramban.',
    'Ultimately, this means that when an attacker deviates from the expected user behavior, the application fails to take appropriate steps to prevent this and, subsequently, fails to handle the situation safely.' => 'Akibatnya, begitu penyerang menyimpang dari alur pengguna normal, aplikasi tidak memiliki mekanisme penahanan atau penanganan aman di sisi server.',
    'Logic flaws are particularly common in overly complicated systems that even the development team themselves do not fully understand. To avoid logic flaws, developers need to understand the application as a whole. This includes being aware of how different functions can be combined in unexpected ways. Developers working on large code bases may not have an intimate understanding of how all areas of the application work. Someone working on one component could make flawed assumptions about how another component works and, as a result, inadvertently introduce serious logic flaws. If the developers do not explicitly document any assumptions that are being made, it is easy for these kinds of vulnerabilities to creep into an application.' => 'Cacat logika makin sering terjadi pada sistem yang sangat rumit ketika tim pengembang di satu komponen membuat asumsi yang keliru mengenai perilaku komponen lain tanpa dokumentasi eksplisit.',
    'What is the impact of business logic vulnerabilities?' => 'Apa dampak kerentanan logika bisnis?',
    "The impact of business logic vulnerabilities can, at times, be fairly trivial. It is a broad category and the impact is highly variable. However, any unintended behavior can potentially lead to high-severity attacks if an attacker is able to manipulate the application in the right way. For this reason, quirky logic should ideally be fixed even if you can't work out how to exploit it yourself. There is always a risk that someone else will be able to." => 'Dampak celah logika sangat beragam, mulai dari hal ringan hingga serangan berisiko kritis. Karena itu, perilaku logika yang janggal sebaiknya tetap diperbaiki meskipun cara eksploitasinya belum langsung terlihat.',
    'Fundamentally, the impact of any logic flaw depends on what functionality it is related to. If the flaw is in the authentication mechanism, for example, this could have a serious impact on your overall security. Attackers could potentially exploit this for privilege escalation, or to bypass authentication entirely, gaining access to sensitive data and functionality. This also exposes an increased attack surface for other exploits.' => 'Besarnya dampak bergantung pada fitur yang terdampak. Cacat logika di sistem autentikasi dapat memicu eskalasi hak akses atau membypass login sepenuhnya.',
    'Flawed logic in financial transactions can obviously lead to massive losses for the business through stolen funds, fraud, and so on.' => 'Sementara pada transaksi keuangan, logika yang rapuh berpotensi menimbulkan kerugian finansial langsung melalui penipuan atau penggelapan dana.',
    'You should also note that even though logic flaws may not allow an attacker to benefit directly, they could still allow a malicious party to damage the business in some way.' => 'Perlu diingat pula bahwa meski penyerang tidak meraup keuntungan langsung, cacat logika tetap bisa dimanfaatkan untuk merusak operasional bisnis.',
    'What are some examples of business logic vulnerabilities?' => 'Apa saja contoh kerentanan logika bisnis?',
    "The best way to understand business logic vulnerabilities is to look at real-world cases and learn from the mistakes that were made. We've provided concrete examples of a variety of common logic flaws, as well as some deliberately vulnerable websites so that you can practice exploiting these vulnerabilities yourself." => 'Cara terbaik memahami kerentanan logika bisnis adalah menelaah contoh kasus nyata dan mempraktikkan eksploitasinya secara langsung.',
    'How to prevent business logic vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah kerentanan logika bisnis',
    'In short, the keys to preventing business logic vulnerabilities are to:' => 'Secara ringkas, kunci mencegah kerentanan logika bisnis adalah:',
    'Make sure developers and testers understand the domain that the application serves' => 'Memastikan pengembang dan penguji memahami domain bisnis yang dilayani aplikasi',
    'Avoid making implicit assumptions about user behavior or the behavior of other parts of the application' => 'Menghindari asumsi tersirat mengenai perilaku pengguna ataupun perilaku komponen aplikasi lain',
    'You should identify what assumptions you have made about the server-side state and implement the necessary logic to verify that these assumptions are met. This includes making sure that the value of any input is sensible before proceeding.' => 'Identifikasi setiap asumsi atas status server dan pastikan ada validasi eksplisit di sisi server untuk memverifikasi kelayakan masukan sebelum proses dilanjutkan.',
    'It is also important to make sure that both developers and testers are able to fully understand these assumptions and how the application is supposed to react in different scenarios. This can help the team to spot logic flaws as early as possible. To facilitate this, the development team should adhere to the following best practices wherever possible:' => 'Seluruh tim juga perlu memiliki pemahaman bersama atas skenario yang diizinkan aplikasi. Terapkan praktik berikut selama pengembangan:',
    'Maintain clear design documents and data flows for all transactions and workflows, noting any assumptions that are made at each stage.' => 'Pelihara dokumentasi desain dan diagram aliran data yang jelas untuk seluruh transaksi beserta asumsi di tiap tahapannya.',
    "Write code as clearly as possible. If it's difficult to understand what is supposed to happen, it will be difficult to spot any logic flaws. Ideally, well-written code shouldn't need documentation to understand it. In unavoidably complex cases, producing clear documentation is crucial to ensure that other developers and testers know what assumptions are being made and exactly what the expected behavior is." => 'Tulis kode sejelas mungkin agar alur logika mudah diaudit; bila kompleksitas tak terhindarkan, lengkapi dengan dokumentasi perilaku yang diharapkan.',
    'Note any references to other code that uses each component. Think about any side-effects of these dependencies if a malicious party were to manipulate them in an unusual way.' => 'Catat setiap ketergantungan antarkomponen dan evaluasi efek samping yang mungkin terjadi apabila salah satu komponen menerima manipulasi tak lazim.',
    "Due to the relatively unique nature of many logic flaws, it is easy to brush them off as a one-time mistake due to human error and move on. However, as we've demonstrated, these flaws are often the result of bad practices in the initial phases of building the application. Analyzing why a logic flaw existed in the first place, and how it was missed by the team, can help you to spot weaknesses in your processes. By making minor adjustments, you can increase the likelihood that similar flaws will be cut off at the source or caught earlier in the development process." => 'Jangan menganggap cacat logika sekadar kesalahan tunggal. Menelusuri akar penyebabnya membantu tim memperbaiki proses pengembangan agar bug serupa dapat dicegah sejak dini.',

    // Examples page
    'Business logic vulnerabilities are relatively specific to the context in which they occur. However, although individual instances of logic flaws differ hugely, they can share many common themes. In particular, they can be loosely grouped based on the initial mistakes that introduced the vulnerability in the first place.' => 'Kerentanan logika bisnis sangat bergantung pada konteks aplikasinya, namun banyak di antaranya berangkat dari pola kekeliruan awal yang serupa.',
    "In this section, we'll look at examples of some typical mistakes that design and development teams make and show you how they can directly lead to business logic flaws. Whether you're developing your own applications, or auditing existing ones, you can take the lessons learned from these examples and apply the same critical thinking to other applications that you encounter." => 'Bagian ini mengulas kekeliruan desain dan implementasi yang paling sering memicu celah logika bisnis agar Anda dapat menerapkan pola pikir kritis serupa saat membangun atau mengaudit aplikasi lain.',
    'Examples of logic flaws include:' => 'Contoh cacat logika meliputi:',
    '[[A0]]Excessive trust in client-side controls[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Kepercayaan berlebihan pada kontrol sisi klien[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]Failing to handle unconventional input[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Gagal menangani masukan tak lazim[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]Making flawed assumptions about user behavior[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Asumsi keliru terhadap perilaku pengguna[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]Domain-specific flaws[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Celah khusus domain bisnis[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]Providing an encryption oracle[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Menyediakan oracle enkripsi[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]Email address parser discrepancies[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Ketidaksesuaian parser alamat email[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    'Excessive trust in client-side controls' => 'Kepercayaan berlebihan pada kontrol sisi klien',
    'A fundamentally flawed assumption is that users will only interact with the application via the provided web interface. This is especially dangerous because it leads to the further assumption that client-side validation will prevent users from supplying malicious input. However, an attacker can simply use tools such as Burp Proxy to tamper with the data after it has been sent by the browser but before it is passed into the server-side logic. This effectively renders the client-side controls useless.' => 'Anggapan bahwa pengguna hanya berinteraksi melalui antarmuka peramban merupakan asumsi keliru yang berbahaya. Penyerang dapat memodifikasi permintaan memakai proxy pencegat setelah data meninggalkan peramban sehingga validasi sisi klien sama sekali tidak berdaya.',
    'Accepting data at face value, without performing proper integrity checks and server-side validation, can allow an attacker to do all kinds of damage with relatively minimal effort. Exactly what they are able to achieve is dependent on the functionality and what it is doing with the controllable data. In the right context, this kind of flaw can have devastating consequences for both business-related functionality and the security of the website itself.' => 'Menerima data tanpa pemeriksaan integritas serta validasi server memampukan penyerang mengubah nilai penting seperti harga atau peran akun dengan usaha minimal.',
    'Failing to handle unconventional input' => 'Gagal menangani masukan tak lazim',
    'One aim of the application logic is to restrict user input to values that adhere to the business rules. For example, the application may be designed to accept arbitrary values of a certain data type, but the logic determines whether or not this value is acceptable from the perspective of the business. Many applications incorporate numeric limits into their logic. This might include limits designed to manage inventory, apply budgetary restrictions, trigger phases of the supply chain, and so on.' => 'Logika aplikasi bertugas memastikan masukan pengguna tetap patuh pada batasan bisnis, seperti batas stok persediaan atau plafon anggaran.',
    "Let's take the simple example of an online shop. When ordering products, users typically specify the quantity that they want to order. Although any integer is theoretically a valid input, the business logic might prevent users from ordering more units than are currently in stock, for example." => 'Pada toko daring misalnya, meskipun kolom jumlah barang menerima bilangan bulat, aturan bisnis harus melarang pemesanan melebihi stok yang tersedia.',
    'To implement rules like this, developers need to anticipate all possible scenarios and incorporate ways to handle them into the application logic. In other words, they need to tell the application whether it should allow a given input and how it should react based on various conditions. If there is no explicit logic for handling a given case, this can lead to unexpected and potentially exploitable behavior.' => 'Pengembang wajib menentukan secara eksplisit kondisi masukan yang diterima maupun ditolak. Ketiadaan aturan untuk skenario tertentu sering memunculkan celah yang dapat dieksploitasi.',
    "For example, a numeric data type might accept negative values. Depending on the related functionality, it may not make sense for the business logic to allow this. However, if the application doesn't perform adequate server-side validation and reject this input, an attacker may be able to pass in a negative value and induce unwanted behavior." => 'Sebagai contoh, tipe angka mendukung nilai negatif. Bila server tidak menolak bilangan negatif, penyerang bisa memasukkannya untuk membalikkan perhitungan logika.',
    'Consider a funds transfer between two bank accounts. This functionality will almost certainly check whether the sender has sufficient funds before completing the transfer:' => 'Perhatikan logika transfer dana berikut yang memeriksa kecukupan saldo pengirim sebelum memproses transfer:',
    'But if the logic doesn\'t sufficiently prevent users from supplying a negative value in the [[C0]] parameter, this could be exploited by an attacker to both bypass the balance check and transfer funds in the "wrong" direction. If the attacker sent -$1000 to the victim\'s account, this might result in them receiving $1000 from the victim instead. The logic would always evaluate that -1000 is less than the current balance and approve the transfer.' => 'Jika server gagal melarang nilai negatif pada parameter [[C0]], penyerang dapat memindahkan dana ke arah berlawanan. Mengirim -$1000 ke akun korban selalu dianggap lebih kecil dari saldo saat ini, sehingga sistem justru menarik $1000 dari korban ke akun penyerang.',
    'Simple logic flaws like this can be devastating if they occur in the right functionality. They are also easy to miss during both development and testing, especially given that such inputs may be blocked by client-side controls on the web interface.' => 'Cacat sesederhana ini berakibat fatal dan kerap terlewat karena nilai negatif biasanya sudah dicegah oleh antarmuka HTML.',
    "When auditing an application, you should use tools such as Burp Proxy and Repeater to try submitting unconventional values. In particular, try input in ranges that legitimate users are unlikely to ever enter. This includes exceptionally high or exceptionally low numeric inputs and abnormally long strings for text-based fields. You can even try unexpected data types. By observing the application's response, you should try and answer the following questions:" => 'Saat mengaudit aplikasi, uji parameter memakai nilai di luar rentang wajar, seperti angka negatif, angka sangat besar, teks sangat panjang, atau tipe data berbeda, lalu amati hal berikut:',
    'Are there any limits that are imposed on the data?' => 'Apakah terdapat batas nilai yang diterapkan pada data tersebut?',
    'What happens when you reach those limits?' => 'Bagaimana perilaku server ketika batas tersebut dilewati?',
    'Is any transformation or normalization being performed on your input?' => 'Apakah masukan mengalami transformasi atau normalisasi sebelum diproses?',
    "This may expose weak input validation that allows you to manipulate the application in unusual ways. Keep in mind that if you find one form on the target website that fails to safely handle unconventional input, it's likely that other forms will have the same issues." => 'Pengujian ini kerap mengungkap validasi yang lemah. Bila satu formulir bermasalah, kemungkinan besar formulir lain pada situs yang sama memiliki kelemahan serupa.',
    'Making flawed assumptions about user behavior' => 'Membuat asumsi keliru tentang perilaku pengguna',
    "One of the most common root causes of logic vulnerabilities is making flawed assumptions about user behavior. This can lead to a wide range of issues where developers have not considered potentially dangerous scenarios that violate these assumptions. In this section, we'll provide some cautionary examples of common assumptions that should be avoided and demonstrate how they can lead to dangerous logic flaws." => 'Salah satu akar penyebab utama cacat logika adalah berasumsi bahwa pengguna selalu berperilaku tertib. Berikut beberapa contoh asumsi berbahaya yang harus dihindari.',
    "Trusted users won't always remain trustworthy" => 'Pengguna tepercaya tidak selalu tetap tepercaya',
    'Applications may appear to be secure because they implement seemingly robust measures to enforce the business rules. Unfortunately, some applications make the mistake of assuming that, having passed these strict controls initially, the user and their data can be trusted indefinitely. This can result in relatively lax enforcement of the same controls from that point on.' => 'Sebagian aplikasi menerapkan validasi ketat di tahap awal, namun kemudian berasumsi bahwa pengguna serta datanya dapat dipercaya selamanya sehingga melonggarkan pemeriksaan di tahap berikutnya.',
    'If business rules and security measures are not applied consistently throughout the application, this can lead to potentially dangerous loopholes that may be exploited by an attacker.' => 'Jika aturan bisnis dan kontrol keamanan tidak diterapkan secara konsisten di seluruh alur, celah berbahaya pun terbuka.',
    "Users won't always supply mandatory input" => 'Pengguna tidak selalu mengirim parameter wajib',
    'One misconception is that users will always supply values for mandatory input fields. Browsers may prevent ordinary users from submitting a form without a required input, but as we know, attackers can tamper with parameters in transit. This even extends to removing parameters entirely.' => 'Meskipun formulir web menandai kolom tertentu sebagai wajib diisi, penyerang dapat memodifikasi permintaan untuk mengosongkan atau menghapus parameter tersebut sepenuhnya.',
    'This is a particular issue in cases where multiple functions are implemented within the same server-side script. In this case, the presence or absence of a particular parameter may determine which code is executed. Removing parameter values may allow an attacker to access code paths that are supposed to be out of reach.' => 'Hal ini berisiko tinggi apabila satu skrip server menangani beberapa fungsi sekaligus berdasarkan ada tidaknya parameter tertentu.',
    'When probing for logic flaws, you should try removing each parameter in turn and observing what effect this has on the response. You should make sure to:' => 'Saat mencari celah logika, coba hapus setiap parameter satu per satu dan amati perubahannya dengan langkah berikut:',
    'Only remove one parameter at a time to ensure all relevant code paths are reached.' => 'Hapus satu parameter pada satu waktu agar semua jalur logika tercakup.',
    'Try deleting the name of the parameter as well as the value. The server will typically handle both cases differently.' => 'Uji baik penghapusan nilai saja maupun penghapusan nama parameternya sekalian, karena server kerap menanganinya secara berbeda.',
    'Follow multi-stage processes through to completion. Sometimes tampering with a parameter in one step will have an effect on another step further along in the workflow.' => 'Ikuti alur multitahap hingga selesai karena manipulasi di tahap awal bisa berdampak pada tahap akhir.',
    "This applies to both URL and [[C0]] parameters, but don't forget to check the cookies too. This simple process can reveal some bizarre application behavior that may be exploitable." => 'Terapkan teknik ini pada parameter URL, parameter [[C0]], maupun cookie untuk menemukan perilaku aplikasi yang rentan.',
    "Users won't always follow the intended sequence" => 'Pengguna tidak selalu mengikuti urutan alur yang semestinya',
    'Many transactions rely on predefined workflows consisting of a sequence of steps. The web interface will typically guide users through this process, taking them to the next step of the workflow each time they complete the current one. However, attackers won\'t necessarily adhere to this intended sequence. Failing to account for this possibility can lead to dangerous flaws that may be relatively simple to exploit.' => 'Banyak transaksi tersusun atas beberapa langkah berurutan. Penyerang tidak wajib mengikuti urutan tautan di antarmuka dan dapat langsung menembak URL langkah tertentu.',
    'For example, many websites that implement two-factor authentication (2FA) require users to log in on one page before entering a verification code on a separate page. Assuming that users will always follow this process through to completion and, as a result, not verifying that they do, may allow attackers to bypass the 2FA step entirely.' => 'Misalnya pada autentikasi dua faktor (2FA), apabila aplikasi menganggap pengguna pasti melalui halaman verifikasi kode tanpa memeriksa apakah 2FA benar-benar sudah diselesaikan, penyerang bisa langsung mengakses halaman terproteksi setelah langkah pertama.',
    'Making assumptions about the sequence of events can lead to a wide range of issues even within the same workflow or functionality. Using tools like Burp Proxy and Repeater, once an attacker has seen a request, they can replay it at will and use forced browsing to perform any interactions with the server in any order they want. This allows them to complete different actions while the application is in an unexpected state.' => 'Setelah merekam permintaan HTTP, penyerang dapat memutar ulang atau melompati langkah memakai forced browsing dalam urutan acak untuk membawa aplikasi ke kondisi tak terduga.',
    'To identify these kinds of flaws, you should use forced browsing to submit requests in an unintended sequence. For example, you might skip certain steps, access a single step more than once, return to earlier steps, and so on. Take note of how different steps are accessed. Although you often just submit a [[C0]] or [[C1]] request to a specific URL, sometimes you can access steps by submitting different sets of parameters to the same URL. As with all logic flaws, try to identify what assumptions the developers have made and where the attack surface lies. You can then look for ways of violating these assumptions.' => 'Coba lompati tahapan, ulangi satu langkah berkali-kali, atau kembali ke tahap awal lewat permintaan [[C0]] maupun [[C1]] guna membongkar asumsi urutan kerja pengembang.',
    'Note that this kind of testing will often cause exceptions because expected variables have null or uninitialized values. Arriving at a location in a partly defined or inconsistent state is also likely to cause the application to complain. In this case, be sure to pay close attention to any error messages or debug information that you encounter. These can be a valuable source of information disclosure, which can help you fine-tune your attack and understand key details about the back-end behavior.' => 'Pengujian urutan seperti ini sering memicu exception akibat variabel yang belum terinisialisasi. Cermati setiap pesan error karena dapat membocorkan petunjuk cara kerja backend.',
    'Domain-specific flaws' => 'Celah khusus domain bisnis',
    'In many cases, you will encounter logic flaws that are specific to the business domain or the purpose of the site.' => 'Sering kali cacat logika terkait erat dengan aturan bisnis spesifik tempat situs tersebut beroperasi.',
    'The discounting functionality of online shops is a classic attack surface when hunting for logic flaws. This can be a potential gold mine for an attacker, with all kinds of basic logic flaws occurring in the way discounts are applied.' => 'Fitur diskon dan kupon pada toko daring merupakan sasaran klasik pencari celah logika.',
    "For example, consider an online shop that offers a 10% discount on orders over $1000. This could be vulnerable to abuse if the business logic fails to check whether the order was changed after the discount is applied. In this case, an attacker could simply add items to their cart until they hit the $1000 threshold, then remove the items they don't want before placing the order. They would then receive the discount on their order even though it no longer satisfies the intended criteria." => 'Contohnya, toko memberi diskon 10% untuk belanja di atas $1000. Jika logika tidak mengevaluasi ulang syarat setelah isi keranjang diubah, penyerang cukup menambah barang hingga $1000, mengaktifkan diskon, lalu menghapus barang sebelum checkout.',
    'You should pay particular attention to any situation where prices or other sensitive values are adjusted based on criteria determined by user actions. Try to understand what algorithms the application uses to make these adjustments and at what point these adjustments are made. This often involves manipulating the application so that it is in a state where the applied adjustments do not correspond to the original criteria intended by the developers.' => 'Perhatikan setiap fitur yang mengubah harga atau poin berdasarkan tindakan pengguna, lalu pahami kapan perhitungan ulang dilakukan agar ketidaksesuaian syarat dapat dimanfaatkan.',
    'To identify these vulnerabilities, you need to think carefully about what objectives an attacker might have and try to find different ways of achieving this using the provided functionality. This may require a certain level of domain-specific knowledge in order to understand what might be advantageous in a given context. To use a simple example, you need to understand social media to understand the benefits of forcing a large number of users to follow you.' => 'Menemukan celah semacam ini menuntut pemahaman atas tujuan penyerang serta konteks bisnis aplikasi, seperti memahami nilai penyalahgunaan fitur pengikut di media sosial.',
    "Without this knowledge of the domain, you may dismiss dangerous behavior because you simply aren't aware of its potential knock-on effects. Likewise, you may struggle to join the dots and notice how two functions can be combined in a harmful way. For simplicity, the examples used in this topic are specific to a domain that all users will already be familiar with, namely an online shop. However, whether you're bug bounty hunting, pentesting, or even just a developer trying to write more secure code, you may at some point encounter applications from less familiar domains. In this case, you should read as much documentation as possible and, where available, talk to subject-matter experts from the domain to get their insight. This may sound like a lot of work, but the more obscure the domain is, the more likely other testers will have missed plenty of bugs." => 'Ketika mengaudit aplikasi dari industri yang kurang familier, pelajari dokumentasi domainnya serta berdiskusilah dengan ahli terkait; semakin khusus suatu domain, semakin besar peluang bug logika terlewat oleh penguji lain.',
    'Providing an encryption oracle' => 'Menyediakan oracle enkripsi',
    'Dangerous scenarios can occur when user-controllable input is encrypted and the resulting ciphertext is then made available to the user in some way. This kind of input is sometimes known as an "encryption oracle". An attacker can use this input to encrypt arbitrary data using the correct algorithm and asymmetric key.' => 'Situasi berbahaya muncul saat masukan pengguna dienkripsi oleh server lalu hasilnya dikembalikan ke pengguna (disebut encryption oracle), sehingga penyerang dapat mengenkripsi data sembarang menggunakan kunci sah aplikasi.',
    'This becomes dangerous when there are other user-controllable inputs in the application that expect data encrypted with the same algorithm. In this case, an attacker could potentially use the encryption oracle to generate valid, encrypted input and then pass it into other sensitive functions.' => 'Hal ini menjadi kritis jika ada fitur lain yang memercayai data terenkripsi dengan kunci dan algoritma yang sama, seperti token sesi atau cookie terenkripsi.',
    'This issue can be compounded if there is another user-controllable input on the site that provides the reverse function. This would enable the attacker to decrypt other data to identify the expected structure. This saves them some of the work involved in creating their malicious data but is not necessarily required to craft a successful exploit.' => 'Risikonya berlipat apabila tersedia fitur lain yang bertindak sebagai decryption oracle sehingga struktur plaintext aslinya ikut terbaca.',
    'The severity of an encryption oracle depends on what functionality also uses the same algorithm as the oracle.' => 'Tingkat keparahan encryption oracle bergantung pada seberapa sensitif fitur lain yang berbagi algoritma dan kunci enkripsi yang sama.',
    'Email address parser discrepancies' => 'Ketidaksesuaian parser alamat email',
    'Some websites parse email addresses to extract the domain and determine which organization the email owner belongs to. While this process may initially seem straightforward, it is actually very complex, even for valid RFC-compliant addresses.' => 'Beberapa situs mem-parsing alamat email untuk mengekstrak domain organisasi penggunanya. Meskipun tampak sederhana, standar format alamat email RFC sangatlah kompleks.',
    'Discrepancies in how email addresses are parsed can undermine this logic. These discrepancies arise when different parts of the application handle email addresses differently.' => 'Perbedaan cara parsing antara modul validasi dengan modul pengiriman atau registrasi dapat melemahkan pembatasan domain tersebut.',
    "An attacker can exploit these discrepancies using encoding techniques to disguise parts of the email address. This enables the attacker to create email addresses that pass initial validation checks but are interpreted differently by the server's parsing logic." => 'Penyerang memakai teknik penyandian atau format khusus agar alamat email lolos pengecekan domain awal, namun diarahkan ke kotak masuk berbeda oleh komponen pemroses berikutnya.',
    'The main impact of email address parser discrepancies is unauthorized access. Attackers can register accounts using seemingly valid email addresses from restricted domains. This enables them to gain access to sensitive areas of the application, such as admin panels or restricted user functions.' => 'Dampak utamanya adalah akses tidak sah karena penyerang dapat mendaftarkan akun seolah berasal dari domain internal perusahaan atau domain terlarang.',
    'For detailed information on email parsing discrepancies, including how they can be exploited, see the [[A0]]Splitting the Email Atom: Exploiting Parsers to Bypass Access Controls[[/A0]] whitepaper by Gareth Heyes of the SecDevLab Research team.' => 'Untuk penjelasan mendalam beserta teknik eksploitasinya, baca makalah [[A0]]Splitting the Email Atom: Exploiting Parsers to Bypass Access Controls[[/A0]] oleh Gareth Heyes dari tim SecDevLab Research.',
];
